# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for /home/siyuchen/STM32
# STM32CubeIDE workspaces (workspace_1.13.2, workspace_2.2.0) + vendored ST
# packages (X-CUBE-53L9A1, STM32CubeH5)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# resource/STM32CubeH5 is already its own git repository
# (github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeH5, ~1.2GB, has its own remote).
# Don't let this repo try to track its contents. If you actually want it
# linked from here, add it as a proper submodule instead of relying on this
# rule: `git submodule add https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeH5.git resource/STM32CubeH5`
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
resource/STM32CubeH5/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STM32CubeIDE / Eclipse CDT build output directories.
#
# Deliberately NOT blanket-ignoring *.bin/*.hex/*.elf/*.a/*.s by extension -
# this tree has legitimate vendor-shipped files with those same extensions
# living outside build folders (the official prebuilt reference image at
# .../53L9A1_PostprocessSingle/Binary/*.bin, RoT-provisioning .bin/.hex test
# data, startup_*.s assembly sources, prebuilt middleware .a libraries).
# Ignoring the whole build-output directory instead is precise and avoids
# accidentally excluding any of those.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Debug/
Release/

# Generated object/build-report files with extensions that are unambiguously
# always generated (never legitimate hand-authored or vendor-shipped source
# in this tree) - a safety net for anything that ever lands outside
# Debug/Release.
*.o
*.obj
*.su
*.cyclo
*.map
*.list
*.d

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Eclipse / STM32CubeIDE workspace metadata - machine-specific, regenerated,
# large (e.g. workspace_1.13.2/.metadata, workspace_2.2.0/.metadata).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.metadata/
.recommenders/
RemoteSystemsTempFiles/

# Per-project IDE indexer/discovery settings cache - often contains
# machine-specific absolute paths, regenerated automatically when a project
# is reopened. Comment this out if you'd rather keep it tracked for
# project-setup consistency across machines.
.settings/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python (Utilities/vl53l9_visualizer.py and any future PC-side tooling)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session backup files left behind from firmware A/B debugging (e.g.
# Src/*.with-visualizer.bak under X-CUBE-53L9A1) - harmless clutter, not
# meant to be committed. Delete them or leave them; either way they won't
# get picked up.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.orig

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor cruft
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
*.swo

# Serial captures written into the repo root by capture_logs.sh / capture_stm32.sh. These are
# throwaway debugging artifacts, regenerated on every run, and the STM32 ones are large (the
# 3Mbaud stream is binary visualizer frames interleaved with text).
/stm32.log
/stm32*.log
/stm32*.log.raw
/stm32_raw.bin
/xiao.log
/xiao*.log
/full.log
